ervise <id>`. If it is dead, call `write_cancelled` directly.\n\nP3 src/cli.rs:416–426 — If the `supersededBy` rewrite fails after B has spawned, `resume` exits 1 without printing B's id, so B is orphaned and running. Fix: print the id and warn, or exit 0.\n\nP3 src/cli.rs:356,369 — The unknown-model error is built twice in `resume`, and the `(_, None)` arm duplicates the `resolve_model` branch. Fix: keep one path, reusing the message from `run` (cli.rs:251).\n\nP3 src/status_record.rs:175 — `write_cancelled` hardcodes `\"backend\": \"cursor\"`. The same string appears at line 142, so this matches the current cursor-only code, but it breaks once the pi and claude backends land.\n\nP3 tests — The SIGKILL escalation path (hung supervisor, `child_pids`, `write_cancelled`) has no test, and the agent-STATUS guard (below) has none either.\n\nYour question: an agent's own `STATUS: CANCELLED` line cannot set the job status. `RunStatus::parse` (src/types.rs:132) now accepts CANCELLED and STALLED. But `derive_status` (src/output.rs:13) also requires `RUN_STATUSES.contains(..)`, and that list is unchanged at 5 entries. So the line falls through to Done or Error. The safeguard is that second check, not `parse`. The doc comment at src/types.rs:97 (\"never parsed\") is wrong for `parse` itself. Fix: add an output.rs test, or drop the two arms from `parse`.\n\nSpec: every acceptance criterion has an e2e test except the SIGKILL fallback noted above.\n\nSTATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS","ttft_ms":1809,"type":"result","duration_ms":39050,"uuid":"274eac1c-e106-4d25-9c24-1630a44672cb","ttft_stream_ms":1090,"time_to_request_ms":381,"first_content_frame_ms":1090,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
